From c452d1ceae71eeb1142d2f004016471e7df63481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:10:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] port: x86 AVX512-VNNI repack GEMV/GEMM for Q1_0 and Q2_0

The declared head of the slot. Before this, batched CPU mul_mat for Q1_0/Q2_0
fell back to per-row vec_dot on x86: Q2_0 had no repack path at all and Q1_0
only the Arm one from the previous commit.

Adds block_q2_0x4 (4-row, 8-byte-chunk interleave) with generic repack/gemv/gemm,
AVX512-VNNI gemv+gemm kernels for the existing q1_0 4x8 layout and the new q2_0
4x8 layout, and the repack-type selection for both formats. sum(qy) is computed
once per activation sub-block and the horizontal reduction once per output tile.

CONFLICT PREDICTION FALSIFIED. The slot sweep rated this HIGH risk and called a
textual conflict with our PowerInfer repack carve-out 56e975ed4 'CONFIRMED, not
speculative', both touching ggml_repack_get_optimal_repack_type(). It applied
with zero conflicts. The reason is structural, not luck: the carve-out is an
early return-nullptr block at the very TOP of the function keyed on tensor NAME,
while this commit appends type arms at the BOTTOM of the if/else chain and adds
traits instances in the declaration block. The hunks are hundreds of lines apart
with unrelated context.

Behaviour of the carve-out is UNCHANGED, and verified by reading the merged
function rather than assumed: the carve-out still executes first, still returns
nullptr for ffn_*_exps under EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH / GENERATE_EXPERT_BUNDLE, and
does so before any type test. For every tensor that is not Q1_0 or Q2_0 the
function is byte-identical to before; those two types previously fell through to
the terminal return nullptr, so the only behaviour delta is confined to them.

g64 ONLY, structurally. Every kernel here is hard-wired to QK2_0 == 64 /
QK1_0 == 128 and to block_q2_0x4 == block<2,4>, whose size derives from
QK_0<2>() == QK2_0. Our GGML_TYPE_Q2_0_G128 (type-id 43, 128 values/block) did
not exist when this was written. Explicit guarding lands in the next commit.

